{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Speak, etc. and you shall say.</b> Since this involves both the obligation of the commandment and also a distinction and honor drawn from it, therefore it says both speaking (dibbur) and saying (amirah)." "<b>And they shall make for themselves, etc.</b> The reason it said the letter vav at the beginning of the matter is, according to what they of blessed memory said, which I wrote in connection with the verse ״וַיֹּאמֶר״ — that Moses said to HaShem: on weekdays they don tefillin and remember, etc., until here. Therefore, when He came to say to him that they should make tzitzit, there is room to err that this commandment would take the place of tefillin — whether one wishes to don tefillin, whether one wishes to don tzitzit without tefillin, even on other days, since through one of them it would suffice for remembrance of the commandments. Therefore He said <b>and they shall make</b> — the vav adds, that the commandment of tefillin stands in its place, and the commandment of tzitzit is added." "<b>throughout their generations, and they shall give, etc.</b> It was necessary to say <b>throughout their generations</b>, since this commandment came only for remembrance of the commandments when one sees it, reason would suggest that when a holy and pure generation comes that does not need this remembrance, there would be no need for tzitzit — Scripture therefore states <b>throughout their generations.</b>" "Further, it may intend to raise the question of why He wrote <b>throughout their generations</b> in the middle of the details of the commandment. Now, since in the commandment of tzitzit there are two things — the white and the blue (techelet): the white exists at all times, while the techelet has times when it is unavailable — HaShem in His wisdom said <b>throughout their generations</b> before the remembrance of the techelet, to say that the white is for all their generations, but techelet, when it is unavailable, there is no obligation in it. And although techelet does not prevent the white nor the white the techelet (Menachot 38a), nevertheless the white is available for all generations without interruption, unlike the techelet."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:51.707044780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}